[demo-presentation] Make the selected consequence legible (notstarted)
Files: crates/caravan-sample/src/render.rs; crates/caravan-sample/src/host/**; crates/caravan-sample/src/bin/**; proposals/rendering-contract.md
Do: Present the selected anchor observations through minimal fire-and-forget render output and target-local presentation. Every visible value must be sourced by the selected GameState; keep render production as GameState + Tau -> RenderOutput and keep the output downstream of authoritative state.
Accept: A user can observe the selected anchor behavior in the native demo; equal GameState/Tau inputs remain deterministic; no auxiliary renderer input or view context is introduced; rendering does not become an interaction authority; and each visible value has a named GameState source.
-> demo-composition
---
[gameplay-evidence] Add gameplay acceptance evidence (notstarted)
Files: crates/caravan-sample/tests/**; crates/caravan-sample/snapshots/**; evidence/clause-to-test.md; proposals/demo-gameplay.md
Do: Add a deterministic trace and focused runtime/manual evidence for the selected anchor slice, including parent isolation and exact temporal behavior where relevant.
Accept: The selected anchor slice is reproducible from a documented command or sequence; authoritative changes are visible in immutable query results; failure/no-op behavior is explicit; and existing anchor, conformance, purity, and host evidence remains green.
-> demo-presentation
---
[boundary-polish] Polish only concrete exposed boundaries (notstarted)
Files: crates/**; proposals/**; evidence/**
Do: Apply the smallest API, error, persistence, or abstraction improvements demanded by the selected gameplay evidence. Keep engine and demo ownership honest; promote a boundary only when a second concrete composition or consumer demonstrates the need.
Accept: Every polish change names the observed requirement and preserves the demo's immutable-worldline semantics; no speculative genericization is introduced.
-> gameplay-evidence
